## Where to find it

Attendance lives under the **My Class** and **Attendance** sections of the staff dashboard.
This dashboard is shared by every institute — whichever institute you're logged into, the
screens are the same; only the terminology changes (see
[Institute Branding](/docs/shared-institute-branding) for why some institutes say "School" and
others say "Kindergarten").

## Marking attendance

- Open **My Class → Attendance** to see today's roster for a class.
- Mark each student present, absent, or late, then save.
- **Live** attendance and the **Report / Filter** views let you look back at past days or
  export a range for a class.

## Why you might not be able to edit a class

Whether you can view or edit a class's attendance depends on your access level for that class,
not just whether you're a teacher:

- **Editable** — you're the assigned class teacher, or the class is in your assigned-classes list.
- **Read-only** — you can see the roster and history but can't change entries. This usually means
  you're covering or observing the class rather than being its assigned teacher.
- **No access** — the class doesn't show up for you at all.

If a class you expect to see is missing, or shows as read-only when you think it shouldn't, ask
your school admin to check your class assignment in **Teachers** rather than assuming it's a bug.

